Package: wsh-openglide
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: Glide 2/3 to OpenGL wrapper for the qemu-3dfx Glide pass-through
 OpenGLide from kjliew/qemu-xtra, the fork kept in step with qemu-3dfx: the
 host side of the 3dfx Glide pass-through of qemu-system-x86_64-3dfx in the
 wsh-pve pve-qemu-kvm package. A Windows 9x or DOS guest's Glide calls arrive
 in QEMU, which loads libglide2x.so (or libglide3x.so for a Glide 3 guest) and
 renders them with OpenGL into its SDL window.
 .
 The libraries are installed under their unversioned names in the multiarch
 library directory, where QEMU's dlopen() looks for them. Without this package
 a guest's Glide driver finds no Glide device; the Mesa/OpenGL pass-through
 doesn't need it.
 .
 Built with the X11/GLX platform (configure --disable-sdl), as qemu-3dfx
 expects.
